ica, and internationally. It operates through three segments: Truck, Parts, and Financial Services. The Truck segment designs, manufactures, and distributes trucks for the over-the-road and off-highway hauling of commercial and consumer goods; and diesel engine products. It sells its trucks through a network of independent dealers under the Kenworth, Peterbilt, and DAF nameplates. The Parts segment distributes aftermarket parts for trucks and related commercial vehicles. The Financial Services segment conducts full-service leasing operations under the PacLease trade name, as well as provides finance and leasing products and services to customers and dealers. This segment offers equipment financing and administrative support services for its franchisees; retail loan and leasing services for small, medium, and large commercial trucking companies, as well as independent owners/operators and other businesses; and truck inventory financing services to independent dealers. In addition, this segment offers loans and leases directly to customers for the acquisition of trucks and related equipment; and operates its own full-service lease outlets. The company manufactures and markets industrial winches under the Braden, Carco, and Gearmatic nameplates. PACCAR Inc was founded in 1905 and is headquartered in Bellevue, Washington.","ceo_bio":"Mr. R. Preston Feight | CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 25K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $142K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $931 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["PACCAR Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $56.2B market cap on $28.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -0% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 24% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 16-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $3.7B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.86\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 8.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 18% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","38 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is PACCAR (PCAR) Undervalued On Its Parts Growth And 2026 Sales Guidance?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-pcar/paccar/news/is-paccar-pcar-undervalued-on-its-parts-growth-and-2026-sale","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794590165.953,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.868,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Is Paccar (NASDAQ:PCAR) Logging Record Parts Revenue?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/industrial/is-paccar-nasdaqpcar-logging-record-parts-revenue","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794402540.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"PACCAR (PCAR) Stock Still Looks Undervalued After Its 113% Run","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/paccar-pcar-stock-still-looks-111553591.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794395753.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.784,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"PACCAR (PCAR) Stock May Be 30% Undervalued On Future Cash Flow","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-pcar/paccar/news/paccar-pcar-stock-may-be-30-undervalued-on-future-cash-